# iOS Liquid Glass Design Spec (cookapp) — HARD RULES

Default visual direction: **iOS 26 Liquid Glass** (light + dark), aligned with Apple HIG Materials / Adopting Liquid Glass, **and** Pestle screenshots in `docs/ui-screenshots/`.

Screenshot = layout, hierarchy, brand green, copy.  
Liquid Glass = how floating chrome / materials / motion behave.

## Where Liquid Glass is allowed

**Only the navigation / control layer** that floats above content:

- Floating tab bar + search circle
- Toolbars, circular/pill header buttons
- Popovers, context menus, sheets, FABs over content
- Transient interactive controls (when active)

**Never** apply Liquid Glass to the content layer:

- Recipe grids, ingredient lists, grocery rows, settings list bodies
- Full-screen page backgrounds, large content cards as “glass slabs”
- Stacking glass on glass (no nested frosted panels)

## Material rules

1. **Regular glass** (default) — tab bar, menus, alerts, text-heavy chrome; must keep label/icon legible (blur + adaptive luminosity).
2. **Clear glass** — only small controls over rich media (hero photo buttons). If clear, add sufficient dimming/scrim so controls stay readable.
3. **Low-contrast borders** — hairline / subtle separator on glass; no heavy opaque strokes.
4. **Translucent, not muddy** — content should read through chrome; avoid opaque grey blocks pretending to be glass.
5. **Light + dark** — both appearances required; glass and vibrancy must work in each. No dark-only defaults.
6. **Tint sparingly** — brand green tints labels/active states; do not flood the whole glass surface with opaque brand color.
7. **Tight spacing** — compact chrome padding consistent with screenshots / iOS density; no oversized SaaS padding.
8. **Motion** — fluid morph/appear for menus, sheets, tab selection (2–3 intentional motions minimum on visually led surfaces). Honor Reduce Motion / Reduce Transparency / Increase Contrast: degrade to solid/legible fallbacks, do not break layout.

## Control states (every interactive control)

Must define once in the kit: **default · hover · active · disabled · loading**.  
Missing states = QA fail.

## Conflict resolution

| Conflict | Winner |
|----------|--------|
| Screenshot layout vs invented layout | Screenshot |
| Shared chrome material vs flat opaque clone | Liquid Glass (regular/clear as above) |
| Brand green accents vs system multicolor | Brand green (Pestle), on glass — not instead of glass |
| Status bar / Dynamic Island / keyboard | Ignore (never implement) |

## Forbidden

- Generic SaaS card stacks, purple/glow AI themes, cream+terracotta defaults
- Opaque solid tab bars that ignore screenshot frosted glass
- Glass used as full-page wallpaper or content-card fill
- Shipping UI without light **and** dark pass when chrome is involved
